%S A397964 0,136,560,1464,3040,5480,8976,13720,19904,27720,37360,49016,62880,
%T A397964 79144,98000,119640,144256,172040,203184,237880,276320,318696,365200,
%U A397964 416024,471360,531400,596336,666360,741664,822440,908880,1001176,1099520,1204104,1315120
%N A397964 Number of points with even coordinate sum in the 4-dimensional hypercube [-n,n]^4 having an odd number of lattice neighbors inside the hypercube.
%C A397964 Points with an odd number of interior neighbors are exactly those with an odd number of coordinates equal to +-n. In even dimensions a corner has an even number of extremal coordinates and so is never counted, at any n; there is therefore no parity defect and the sequence is a single polynomial, in contrast to the odd-dimensional cases such as A398862. These considerations lead to a formula for a(n), proved by the stratification argument given in A397966.
%H A397964 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (4,-6,4,-1).
%F A397964 a(n) = 32*n^3 - 48*n^2 + 56*n - 40.
%F A397964 G.f.: 8*x^2*(17 + 2*x + 5*x^2)/(1 - x)^4.
%F A397964 E.g.f.: 8*(5 + exp(x)*(4*x^3 + 6*x^2 + 5*x - 5)). - _Stefano Spezia_, Aug 20 2026
%e A397964 For n = 2 the hypercube [-2,2]^4 has 625 points, of which a(2) = 136 have even coordinate sum and an odd number of the 8 lattice neighbors still inside.
%o A397964 (PARI) a(n) = 32*n^3 - 48*n^2 + 56*n - 40
%o A397964 (Python) def a(n): return 32*n**3 - 48*n**2 + 56*n - 40
%Y A397964 Cf. A397966, A398862.
%K A397964 nonn,easy,new
%O A397964 1,2
%A A397964 _Sathish Kumar_, Aug 13 2026
